# Build toolchain, for the case where Kivy has to be COMPILED rather than
# downloaded.
#
# docs/design/runtime-inventory.md, the single most consequential finding on
# armhf: the installed Kivy-2.3.1.dist-info/WHEEL read "Tag:
# cp313-cp313-linux_armv7l" and NO SUCH WHEEL EXISTS ON PyPI, so it was built
# from sdist on the device. ospi never pays this cost -- on its Python version
# rotary-controller-python pulls a prebuilt wheel -- which is why its stage
# installs runtime SDL2 only. On arm64, a prebuilt cp313-cp313-linux_aarch64
# wheel exists, so Kivy is no longer compiled here; the -dev packages below
# stay anyway, a judgment call recorded in DECISIONS.md.
#
# build-essential, pkg-config and python3-venv already come from upstream
# stage2/01-sys-tweaks; the -dev set does not.

libsdl2-dev
libsdl2-image-dev
libsdl2-mixer-dev
libsdl2-ttf-dev
libmtdev-dev
python3-dev

# Present via stage2, named here because the Kivy build fails without them and
# the harness asserts on this contract.
build-essential
pkg-config

# Cython arrives transiently through PEP 517 build isolation. It is deliberately
# NOT installed as a package -- it is not one on the live machine either.
